IO-45: read evaporation from a runoff interface file in the units it was written

RunoffInterfaceFile::writeResults() writes evaporation as evap_loss *
UCF(EVAPRATE) (in/day or mm/day), but readResults() divided it by
UCF(RAINFALL) (in/hr or mm/hr), copying legacy runoff_readFromFile() on
purpose. A USE RUNOFF run reported 24 times the evaporation of the run that
wrote the file. Divide by UCF(EVAPRATE), and correct the comments.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-45_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/hydrology/RunoffInterface.cpp b/src/engine/hydrology/RunoffInterface.cpp
index 2d2f9d3..3f38810 100644
--- a/src/engine/hydrology/RunoffInterface.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/hydrology/RunoffInterface.cpp
@@ -208,15 +208,14 @@ bool RunoffInterfaceFile::readResults(SimulationContext& ctx, double* dt_out) {
             return false;
 
         // Restore subcatchment state from file, converting the user-unit
-        // record values back to internal units exactly as legacy
-        // runoff_readFromFile does — including its evap asymmetry (written
-        // ×UCF(EVAPRATE) but read ÷UCF(RAINFALL), a deliberate legacy-parity
-        // quirk). Snow depth / GW elev / soil moisture have no refactored
+        // record values back to internal units with the factors they were
+        // written with (evaporation in in/day or mm/day: UCF(EVAPRATE)).
+        // Snow depth / GW elev / soil moisture have no refactored
         // per-subcatch state and are skipped.
         const int us = unit_system_;
         const double qcf = ucf::Qcf[flow_units_];
         ctx.subcatches.evap_loss[uj]  = static_cast<double>(buf_[2])
-                                        / ucf::Ucf[ucf::RAINFALL][us];
+                                        / ucf::Ucf[ucf::EVAPRATE][us];
         ctx.subcatches.infil_loss[uj] = static_cast<double>(buf_[3])
                                         / ucf::Ucf[ucf::RAINFALL][us];
         ctx.subcatches.runoff[uj]     = static_cast<double>(buf_[4]) / qcf;
